prompt:
Validate this Normalizer transform against its metadata and requirements.

The voucher and cash tender accounting export. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. void receipt: when payment_status equals "VOID", export nothing.
2. invalid voucher: when voucher < 0, export ERROR (-voucher).
3. reservation: when payment_status equals "RESERVE", export nothing.
4. refund: when payment_status equals "REFUND", export REFUND (-sale_value).
5. reviewed split tender: when sale_value > voucher and voucher > 0 and review, export VOUCHER (voucher) followed by CASH (sale_value-voucher) followed by AUDIT (0).
6. voucher overpayment: when voucher > sale_value, export VOUCHER (sale_value) followed by CHANGE (voucher-sale_value).
7. mixed tender: when voucher > 0, export VOUCHER (voucher) followed by CASH (sale_value-voucher).
8. cash only: when otherwise, export CASH (sale_value).

Input 0 (In_voucher_tender_0): tender_id stores a string value; must be present
sale_value stores a decimal value; must be present
review stores a boolean value; must be present
payment_status stores a string value; must be present
voucher stores a decimal value; must be present
tender_note stores a string value; may be absent.
Output 0 (Out_voucher_tender_0): tender_ref stores a string value; must be present
tender_leg stores a string value; must be present
value stores a decimal value; must be present.
Each source ID is unique; carry tender_id into tender_ref. Entry labels go in tender_leg, values in value.

```ctl
//#CTL2
string voucher_reference;
string[] voucher_actions = [];
decimal[] voucher_values = [];
function void post_voucher(string label, decimal value) {
    append(voucher_actions, label);
    append(voucher_values, value);
}
function integer count() {
    voucher_actions = [];
    voucher_values = [];
    voucher_reference = $in.0.tender_id;
    /* Priority table:
       1. void receipt -> 0 rows
       2. invalid voucher -> 1 rows
       3. reservation -> 0 rows
       4. refund -> 1 rows
       5. reviewed split tender -> 3 rows
       6. voucher overpayment -> 2 rows
       7. mixed tender -> 2 rows
       8. cash only -> 1 rows
    */
    if ($in.0.payment_status == "VOID") {
        return 0; // void receipt
    }
    else if ($in.0.voucher < 0d) {
        post_voucher("ERROR", -$in.0.voucher);
        return 1; // invalid voucher
    }
    else if ($in.0.payment_status == "RESERVE") {
        return 0; // reservation
    }
    else if ($in.0.payment_status == "REFUND") {
        post_voucher("REFUND", -$in.0.sale_value);
        return 1; // refund
    }
    else if ($in.0.sale_value > $in.0.voucher && $in.0.voucher > 0d && $in.0.review) {
        post_voucher("VOUCHER", $in.0.voucher);
        post_voucher("CASH", $in.0.sale_value-$in.0.voucher);
        post_voucher("AUDIT", 0d);
        return 3; // reviewed split tender
    }
    else if ($in.0.voucher > $in.0.sale_value) {
        post_voucher("VOUCHER", $in.0.sale_value);
        post_voucher("CHANGE", $in.0.voucher-$in.0.sale_value);
        return 2; // voucher overpayment
    }
    else if ($in.0.voucher >= 0d) {
        post_voucher("VOUCHER", $in.0.voucher);
        post_voucher("CASH", $in.0.sale_value-$in.0.voucher);
        return 2; // mixed tender
    }
    else if (true) {
        post_voucher("CASH", $in.0.sale_value);
        return 1; // cash only
