The product return settlement export. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. abandoned claim: when disposition equals "ABANDON", export nothing.
2. rejected inspection: when disposition equals "REJECT", export REJECT (0).
3. no value: when item_value equals 0, export nothing.
4. exchange: when disposition equals "EXCHANGE", export RETURN (item_value) followed by REPLACEMENT (-freight).
5. restocking with audit: when disposition equals "RESTOCK" and audit, export CREDIT (item_value*(100-20)/100) followed by FEE (item_value*20/100) followed by AUDIT (0).
6. freight recovery: when freight > item_value, export FREIGHT (freight-item_value).
7. restocking without audit: when disposition equals "RESTOCK", export CREDIT (item_value*(100-20)/100) followed by FEE (item_value*20/100).
8. simple credit: when otherwise, export CREDIT (item_value-freight).

Input 0 (In_return_settlement_0): return_id (string; required); disposition (string; required); item_value (decimal; required); freight (decimal; required); audit (boolean; required); inspection_note (string; nullable).
