The inventory transfer journals export. Listed rules have precedence from top to bottom. Parentheses give the exact value for each named entry.

1. void transfer: when ticket equals "VOID", export nothing.
2. damaged units: when requested < 0, export REJECT (-requested).
3. same bin: when ticket equals "SAME", export nothing.
4. quarantine: when ticket equals "QUARANTINE", export HOLD (requested) followed by NOTICE (0).
5. short pick: when available < requested, export PICK (available) followed by SHORT (requested-available).
6. large audited move: when requested >= 10 and trace, export OUT (-requested) followed by IN (requested) followed by TRACE (0).
7. ordinary paired move: when ticket equals "MOVE", export OUT (-requested) followed by IN (requested).
8. inventory sample: when otherwise, export SAMPLE (requested+available).

Input 0 (In_bin_transfer_0): move_id:string (required); ticket:string (required); requested:decimal (required); available:decimal (required); trace:boolean (required); bin_note:string (nullable).
Output 0 (Out_bin_transfer_0): move_ref:string (required); movement:string (required); units:decimal (required).
Each source ID is unique; carry move_id into move_ref. Entry labels go in movement, values in units.

